  "track": "track-07",
  "title": "React state reducer context and action hooks",
  "status": "source-backed-scope-complete",
  "concepts": [
    "State is a component's memory across renders. Each render receives a fixed snapshot; a setter or dispatch schedules later work rather than changing the current variable in place.",
    "useState fits independent state values and direct or functional updates. useReducer centralizes transitions as a pure mapping from state and action to next state.",
    "React queues and batches updates. Functional updater functions compose queued updates when the next value depends on the previous one; objects and arrays should be replaced immutably.",
    "Context passes a value through a subtree without manually threading props through every intermediate component. Consumers subscribe to the nearest provider value.",
    "Actions represent work that may be asynchronous. useActionState stores an Action result and pending state; useOptimistic presents a temporary UI state while an Action is pending.",
    "Hook calls must remain at the top level and in stable order. Custom Hooks compose React behavior while following the same rules."
  ],
